🔹 Step 1: Dataset Used

LIAR Dataset (Politifact statements)

Train / Validation / Test .tsv files

Binary classification derived as:

Fake → pants-fire, false, barely-true, half-true

Genuine → mostly-true, true

Raw files stored in:

data/data_raw/

🔹 Step 2: Dataset Preprocessing

Script:

scripts/preprocess_dataset.py


Preprocessing includes:

Lowercasing text

Removing URLs, numbers, and punctuation

Tokenization using NLTK

Stopword removal

Lemmatization

Mapping labels to Fake / Genuine

Output:

data/processed/cleaned_liar_dataset.csv


Run:

python scripts/preprocess_dataset.py

🔹 Step 3: Model Training

Script:

scripts/train_classifier.py

Model Pipeline

TF-IDF Vectorizer

Unigrams + Bigrams

Max features: 5000

Logistic Regression

Class-balanced

Hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV

Evaluation Metrics

Accuracy

Precision

Recall

F1 Score

ROC-AUC

Confusion Matrix

Metrics are logged and saved to:

results.txt


Artifacts saved to:

models/
 ├── fake_news_model.pkl
 └── vectorizer.pkl


Run:

python scripts/train_classifier.py

🔹 Step 4: ML Inference Service

File:

app/services/ml_service.py


Responsibilities:

Lazy-load model and vectorizer

Validate input text

Vectorize input using TF-IDF

Predict label (Fake / Genuine)

Compute confidence score (percentage)

Output format:

{
  "label": "Fake",
  "confidence": 69.71
}

